**Deviations**
- RED and GREEN landed as one commit: the first `git add -A` swept the fixes into the test commit, and the repo's ddl-pretender pre-commit gate forced the refactor (file ≤400 lines, per-fn complexity caps) before anything could commit. Net: one commit instead of three.
- The RED run exposed two real gaps, fixed as the tests dictated: (1) corpus companions lacked the c1 perl/seed metadata line — inserted after the pin header, **no oracle output bytes re-rendered**; (2) `tools/oracle.pl` couldn't distinguish wrong-version Graph::Easy from not-installed (perl doesn't auto-load the class) — changed to `eval { require Graph::Easy; Graph::Easy->VERSION }`.
- `justfile` FIX made overridable (`${FIX:-tests/fixtures/graph-easy}`) in `oracle-record`/`oracle-verify` so p4 case 5 probes a stale-pinned tempdir corpus without touching the repo tree.
- p4 case 3 targets the *off-checkout* clause (right version, wrong path) because this machine has a cpan-installed Graph::Easy 0.76 — a fully absent checkout surfaces as cpan-copy drift, still a typed c4 error.
- One transient bug during development briefly pointed `oracle.pl record` at `/tmp`; verified no stray `.expected` companions were written there (parser rejected the unparseable inputs before any write).

